{"id":"c-dr-pak--supergains-superset-program","src":"coach","title":"SuperGains (Superset Program)","author":"Dr. Pak","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/coaches/dr-pak/supergains-superset-program","desc":"<p>Created exclusive by Dr. Pak for Boostcamp, this is a 3-day per week superset based program to help you get massive muscles in 8 weeks!</p><p>Watch Dr. Pak's <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EcXYKD52ID0\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">YouTube video</a> about the program.</p><p><strong>Why do a superset program?</strong></p><p>Dr. Pak was part of a team that conducted a study that shows antagonist supersets results in similar increases in muscle growth, strength, and muscle endurance outcomes compared to traditional training. But the superset group only took 44 minutes per workout compared to 69 minutes for the traditional group!</p><p>Several acute studies also showthat antagonist supersets found no impairment in performance compared to traditional training - and, sometimes, even an improvement.</p><p><strong>Who is Dr. Pak?</strong></p><p>Pak Androulakis Korakakis works with Stronger By Science as a Content &amp; Product Manager. As a researcher, Pak did his PhD on \"the minimum effective training dose for powerlifting strength\" and is currently a Visiting Scholar at the Applied Muscle Development Lab at Lehman College in New York City where he researches all things strength and hypertrophy related. As a coach, Pak works with individuals of all sporting and professional backgrounds, from beginner lifters to competitive strength and physique sports athletes.</p><p>You can learn more about Dr. Pak and training information on his <a href=\"https://www.drpak.com/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">website</a>, <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/dr__pak\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">instagram</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@Dr__Pak\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">YouTube channel</a>.</p>","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":45,"joins":2098,"rate":4.2,"rateCount":225,"updated":"2026-10-09T23:16:15.744Z","variations":[{"name":"Default","days":["Push/Pull","Legs","Push/Pull"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":4}],"note":"RIR 0-2"},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":4}],"note":"RIR 0-2"}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Chest Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":4}],"note":"RIR 0-2"},{"n":"Pullover (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":4}],"note":"RIR 0-2"}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":4}],"note":"RIR 0-1"},{"n":"Cable Flexion Row","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":4}],"note":"RIR 0-1"}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Overhead Extension (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":15,"x":3}],"note":"RIR 0-1"},{"n":"Bicep Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":15,"x":3}],"note":"RIR 0-1"}]}],"note":"Recommended rest between each exercise: 20-40 seconds, between each superset: 2-3 minutes"},{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":3}],"note":"RIR 1-3"},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":3}],"note":"RIR 1-3"},{"ss":[{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":5}],"note":"RIR 0-2"},{"n":"Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":5}],"note":"RIR 0-2"}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Straight Leg Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":5}],"note":"RIR 0-2"},{"n":"Cable Crunch","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":5}]}]}],"note":"Recommended rest between each exercise: 20-40 seconds, between each superset: 2-3 minutes"},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Partial Incline Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":4}],"note":"RIR 0-1"},{"n":"Partial Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":4}],"note":"RIR 0-1"}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Deficit Push Up","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":4}],"note":"RIR 0-1"},{"n":"Partial Chin-Up","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":4}],"note":"RIR 0-1 • Bodyweight or assisted • 8-12 reps or AMRAP"}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":3}],"note":"RIR 0-1"},{"n":"